## **4. Next step — generate individual configuration files**

Instead of comparing the entire JSON response, we will extract individual pipeline configurations into separate PROD and DEV directories.

Execute the following on your Mac.

```
cd ~/lma-pipeline-comparison

umask 077

mkdir -p prod-pipelines
mkdir -p dev-pipelines
mkdir -p pipeline-differences
mkdir -p missing-pipelines
```

Copy and paste the entire Perl script below:

```
perl -MJSON::PP <<'PERL'
use strict;
use warnings;

sub load_json {
    my ($file) = @_;
    open my $fh, '<:raw', $file or die "$file: $!";
    local $/;
    return decode_json(<$fh>);
}

sub save_file {
    my ($file, $content) = @_;

    open my $fh, '>:encoding(UTF-8)', $file
        or die "$file: $!";

    print $fh $content;
    close $fh;
}

my $prod = load_json("com-lma-prod-fixed.json");
my $dev  = load_json("non-lma-dev-fixed.json");

for my $id (sort keys %$prod) {

    die "Unexpected pipeline ID: $id\n"
        unless $id =~ /\A[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\z/;

    save_file(
        "prod-pipelines/$id.conf",
        $prod->{$id}{pipeline}
    );

    unless (exists $dev->{$id}) {

        save_file(
            "missing-pipelines/$id.conf",
            $prod->{$id}{pipeline}
        );
    }
}

for my $id (sort keys %$dev) {

    die "Unexpected pipeline ID: $id\n"
        unless $id =~ /\A[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\z/;

    save_file(
        "dev-pipelines/$id.conf",
        $dev->{$id}{pipeline}
    );
}

print "PROD configurations exported: ",
    scalar(keys %$prod), "\n";

print "DEV configurations exported: ",
    scalar(keys %$dev), "\n";

print "Pipeline extraction completed.\n";
PERL
```

## **5. Generate differences for all 34 pipelines automatically**

Execute:

```
for file in prod-pipelines/*.conf; do

    name=$(basename "$file")

    if [ -f "dev-pipelines/$name" ]; then

        if ! cmp -s "$file" "dev-pipelines/$name"; then

            diff -u \
                "dev-pipelines/$name" \
                "$file" \
                > "pipeline-differences/${name%.conf}.diff"

        fi

    fi

done
```

Check the generated files:

```
ls -lrt pipeline-differences/
```

Check the number of difference files:

```
ls pipeline-differences/*.diff | wc -l
```

Expected result based on your comparison:

```
34
```

